# Aesthetic & UX Improvement Plan for Jedi Labs Website

**Vision:** Transform the Jedi Labs website into a visually compelling, modern, and highly usable platform that clearly communicates its identity as an innovative, trustworthy, and state-of-the-art Gen AI solutions provider. This plan emphasizes reusability, consistency, and a refined aesthetic.

**Key Files & Configurations:**
*   Tailwind Configuration: `[tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js)`
*   Global Styles: `[src/index.css](mdc:src/index.css)`
*   Core Button Component: `[src/components/Button.jsx](mdc:src/components/Button.jsx)`
*   Example Card Component: `[src/components/FeaturedApplications/ApplicationCard.jsx](mdc:src/components/FeaturedApplications/ApplicationCard.jsx)` (and other card variants)
*   Header/Navigation: `[src/components/Header.jsx](mdc:src/components/Header.jsx)`
*   Example Hero Component: `[src/features/industries/components/IndustryHero.jsx](mdc:src/features/industries/components/IndustryHero.jsx)`
*   Icon Component: `[src/components/Icon.jsx](mdc:src/components/Icon.jsx)`

---

## Phase 1: Foundational Styles

**Goal:** Establish a consistent and modern visual language through strategic color and typography application.

**1.1. Color Strategy & Application:**
*   **Approach:** Solidify a dark theme by default, leveraging the existing rich neutral and accent color palette in `[tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js)`.
*   **Semantic Color Mapping (Dark Theme Example - to be refined/confirmed):**
    *   `bg-page`: `n-8` (#0E0C15) - Main page background
    *   `bg-card-primary`: `n-7` (#15131D) - Primary card/section background
    *   `bg-card-secondary`: `n-6` (#252134) - Lighter cards or elevated sections
    *   `bg-interactive`: `n-5` (#3F3A52) - Hover states, subtle interactive elements
    *   `bg-accent`: `color-1` (#AC6AFF) - Primary accent for CTAs, highlights
    *   `bg-accent-hover`: Define a slightly darker/lighter shade of `bg-accent`.
    *   `text-high-contrast`: `n-1` (#FFFFFF) - Primary text on dark backgrounds
    *   `text-medium-contrast`: `n-2` (#CAC6DD) - Secondary text, descriptions
    *   `text-low-contrast`: `n-3` (#ADA8C3) - Muted text, captions, placeholders
    *   `text-on-accent`: `n-1` (#FFFFFF) (ensure sufficient contrast if accent is light)
    *   `text-link`: `color-1` (#AC6AFF) or `color-5` (#858DFF) - For inline links.
    *   `border-strong`: `stroke-1` (#26242C) - For distinct separations.
    *   `border-subtle`: `n-5` (#3F3A52) or `n-6` (#252134) - For less prominent borders.
*   **Action:**
    *   Confirm/refine semantic color names and their mappings in `tailwind.config.js` or establish a clear usage convention.
    *   Discuss light theme strategy (if desired).

**1.2. Typography Refinement:**
*   **Font Usage:**
    *   `font-sora`: Confirm as the primary sans-serif font for body text and general UI elements. Ensure consistent application via base styles or utility classes.
    *   `font-grotesk`: Continue using for `.tagline` or similar stylistic text.
    *   `font-code`: Evaluate legibility for `.button`; ensure it aligns with the desired professional aesthetic. Suitable for `.quote` and code snippets.
    *   `font-starjedi`: **Critically review usage.** Restrict to highly specific branding elements (e.g., part of a logo wordmark) and avoid in general UI text, headings, or buttons to maintain a "state-of-the-art" and broadly "trustworthy" feel.
*   **Semantic Text Styles:**
    *   Consistently use the defined utility classes (`.h1` - `.h6`, `.body-1`, `.body-2`, etc. from `[tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js)`).
    *   Review and optimize line heights and letter spacing for readability across all text styles.
*   **Action:**
    *   Adjust font settings in `[tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js)` or `[src/index.css](mdc:src/index.css)` as needed.
    *   Audit components to ensure consistent use of semantic text styles.

